---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const redcircleUrl = 'https://www.redcircle.com/shows/1c89c053-9573-49fe-a9c6-b34f4c6b449d';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Ghost Subie Adventures — the best way to prepare is to go. Roman, his family, and the Ghost: a daily-driven Subaru Forester turned rolling classroom and adventure rig."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
      <h1>The best way to prepare is to go.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Ghost Subie Adventures is built on a simple belief: preparedness isn&rsquo;t paranoia
        &mdash; it&rsquo;s freedom, and the path to preparedness doesn&rsquo;t need to be filled
        with panic and fearmongering.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band-black about-band">
    <img
      src="/images/about-family.jpg"
      alt="Roman, Michelle, and Jonah together outdoors at camp"
      class="about-family-photo"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about-cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I&rsquo;m Roman, the driver behind the wheel and the storyteller behind the miles. What
          started as a love of the outdoors and Subarus turned into a mission to show how
          adventure, skill-building, and real-world readiness go hand in hand.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the peak of COVID, I listened to all the &ldquo;influencers&rdquo; giving
          &ldquo;buy now&rdquo; pitches and bad advice. I got tired of it, so I asked: what if we
          could make preparedness fun? What if the adventures we have on our own and with our
          families could help us all be more prepared? Whether in the city or the wilderness,
          those practical skills can help.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="pull-quote">
          I run a 2022 Subaru Forester that&rsquo;s a daily driver &mdash; and much more.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          It&rsquo;s a rolling classroom. Every trail teaches something. Every breakdown becomes a
          lesson. Every trip sharpens the skills that matter when life gets unpredictable. Out
          here, preparedness isn&rsquo;t about stockpiling fear or flexing gear. It&rsquo;s about
          learning, adapting, and becoming more capable one mile at a time.
        </p>
        <p>
          It&rsquo;s an adventure rig. I&rsquo;m a husband and a dad, and the outdoors is where
          our family connects best. We chase national parks, backroads, lake towns, and quiet
          places where the world slows down. My son gets to see what capability looks like &mdash;
          not in theory, but in practice. How to stay calm. How to solve problems. How to respect
          nature. How to be ready for whatever comes next. And we get to do it while traveling to
          some pretty cool places&hellip; just see for yourself.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ghost Subie Adventures is where I document that journey &mdash; the builds, the gear
          that actually works (and doesn&rsquo;t), the skills that matter, and the adventures that
          test them. It&rsquo;s storytelling with a purpose: showing that preparedness can be fun,
          practical, and family-centered. No fearmongering. No doomsday vibes. Just real-world
          capability built through exploration, curiosity, and miles on the odometer.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you&rsquo;re here, welcome to the ride. Explore the stories, learn the skills, and
          join a community built on adventure, readiness, and the belief that the best way to
          prepare&hellip; is to go.
        </p>
        <p class="about-cta">
          <a href={redcircleUrl} class="btn btn-dark" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hear the podcast &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/field-notes" class="btn btn-outline">Read From the Ghost</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="roman-aside">
        <img
          class="framed"
          src="/images/about-basecamp.jpg"
          alt="Roman leaning on the Ghost beneath the Subaru Base Camp sign"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <h2>Roman &amp; the Ghost</h2>
        <p>San Antonio, Texas. Family camp, Subaru culture, everyday preparedness.</p>
        <p class="pills">
          <span class="pill">Overlanding</span>
          <span class="pill">Podcast</span>
          <span class="pill">Family camp</span>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3 about-cards">
      <a href="/podcast" class="card about-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="card-meta">Podcast</span>
          <h3>Real talk from a real rig</h3>
          <p>Family overlanding, preparedness without panic, and conversations from the campfire.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Listen in &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/field-notes" class="card about-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="card-meta">From the Ghost</span>
          <h3>Written from the driver&rsquo;s seat</h3>
          <p>Rig builds, trip reports, and preparedness lessons earned in the field.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Read the notes &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      <a href="/checklist" class="card about-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="card-meta">Free field guide</span>
          <h3>The Rig-Ready Checklist</h3>
          <p>The exact pre-trip scan we run before family camp.</p>
          <span class="card-link">Get the checklist &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="section center road-cta">
      <h2>Ready to hit the road?</h2>
      <p><a href="/checklist" class="btn btn-dark">Get the Rig-Ready Checklist &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-band {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .about-family-photo {
    max-height: 560px;
    width: auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  .about-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .about-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .pull-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 2.6rem 0;
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }
  .about-cta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .roman-aside img { width: 100%; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .roman-aside h2 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .roman-aside p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; }
  .pills { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .pill {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--paper);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .about-cards { padding: 0 0 1rem; }
  .about-card { text-decoration: none; }
  .about-card:hover { border-color: var(--ink); }
  .road-cta h2 { margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
</style>
